  "_commit": {
    "id": "85f3aa56c9edbb2068213f809b6254c411d19f5b",
    "author": "Ossama Edbali <ossedb@gmail.com>",
    "committer": "Ossama Edbali <ossedb@gmail.com>",
    "message": "perf(check): Read raw spectra serially and slim down examples\n\nSpectra reads mzML files with bpparam(), which on Windows is a SnowParam\nthat starts a new cluster for every call. msPurity parallelises over\nfiles through its own cores argument, so raw data access now uses\nSerialParam. This removes the worker start-ups that took most of the\nWindows test time.\n\nExamples that reran xcms and purityA now load the saved fixtures,\nspectralMatching uses the bundled mini library, and the DIMS and purityX\nexamples work on fewer peaks. Examples no longer write to the working\ndirectory. Legacy tests covered by the golden SQLite dumps are removed;\nthe purityX plot check they held moves to test.7_purityX.R.\n\nBump the version to 1.39.4 with a NEWS entry.\n",
    "time": 1794768191
  },
